/*!
  \page example_cxx_factory_page Iterating over fitting methods with the Factory

  This example uses Ponca::Factory to process the same neighborhood with many compute objects, without writing their
  types:
  - all the methods of the factory are applied in a loop (their state is not kept),
  - the list is filtered to keep the methods that build an implicit primitive and provide a projection operator, but
    no derivatives; the filtered list stores its objects, which are then used to project a point,
  - a method is retrieved by its name (`APSS`).

  Build and run:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_factory
  ./build/examples/cpp/ponca_factory
  \endcode

  See also \ref fitting_factory and \ref fittingreference_factory.

  \include cpp/ponca_factory.cpp
*/
